.TH NEO-NCMP 1 "2026-11-15" "neo-ncmp 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
neo-ncmp \- modern, feature-rich terminal client for MPD
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B neo-ncmp
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fICOMMAND\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B neo-ncmp
is a terminal music client for the Music Player Daemon (MPD). It keeps the
keyboard conventions of ncmpcpp while providing asynchronous library indexing,
live idle updates, fuzzy search, terminal album art, synced lyrics, MPRIS,
scrobbling, a play history, a tag editor, a file browser, and a real-time
visualizer fed by an MPD FIFO or a PipeWire sink monitor.
.PP
With no command it starts the TUI. MPD remains responsible for playback.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-host \fIHOST\fR
Override the configured MPD host.
.TP
.B \-\-port \fIPORT\fR
Override the configured MPD port.
.TP
.B \-\-config \fIPATH\fR
Use an explicit TOML configuration file.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Connect to MPD, print a summary, and exit without starting the TUI.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B check
Same as \fB\-\-check\fR.
.TP
.B status [\-\-json]
Print the current playback state. With \fB\-\-json\fR, emit a machine-readable
object suitable for status bars.
.TP
.B remote \fIACTION\fR
Control MPD without starting the TUI.
.TP
.B ipc \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIVALUE\fR]
Send a JSON line over the running instance's private Unix socket. Commands:
\fBping\fR, \fBstatus\fR, \fBscreen\fR, \fBsearch\fR, \fBaction\fR,
\fBvolume\fR, \fBseek\fR, \fBplaylist\fR, \fBpartition\fR, and
\fBnotify\fR. The socket
defaults to \fI$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/neo-ncmp/socket\fR and mode 0600; configure it
with the \fB[ipc]\fR table.
.SH REMOTE ACTIONS
.TP
.B play, pause, toggle, stop, next, previous
Transport control.
.TP
.B volume \fIVALUE\fR
Absolute 0\-100 or relative with \fB+\fR/\fB\-\fR, e.g. \fB+5\fR.
.TP
.B seek \fISECONDS\fR
Absolute or relative (\fB+10\fR / \fB\-10\fR) seek.
.TP
.B repeat|random|single|consume \fIon|off|toggle\fR
Player options.
.TP
.B shuffle, clear
Queue operations.
.TP
.B partitions
List MPD partitions; the active one is marked with an asterisk.
.TP
.B partition \fINAME\fR
Switch partition, changing the queue and playback state.
.SH SCROBBLE QUEUE
.TP
.B scrobble queue [\-\-json]
List pending offline scrobbles. The Stats screen shows the same queue.
.TP
.B scrobble retry
Retry every queued scrobble once; failures stay queued.
.TP
.B scrobble forget \fIINDEX\fR
Remove one entry by its index from \fBscrobble queue\fR.
.TP
.B playlist \fINAME\fR
Replace the queue with a stored playlist and play it.
.TP
.B output \fIID\fR \fIon|off\fR
Enable or disable an audio output.
.TP
.B status [\-\-json]
Playback status.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The default configuration file is
.IR ~/.config/neo-ncmp/config.toml .
See \fIconfig.example.toml\fR in the distribution for all sections
(\fBmpd\fR, \fBui\fR, \fBlibrary\fR, \fBvisualizer\fR, \fBscrobbling\fR,
\fBstats\fR, \fBsearch\fR, \fBartwork\fR, \fBipc\fR, \fBkeys\fR,
\fBtheme\fR).
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B ?, :, /
Help, command palette, and fuzzy library search.
.TP
.B 1\-9, 0, Tab, Shift-Tab
Queue, Library, Playlists, Outputs, Stats, Lyrics, Visualizer, Tags, History,
Browser; next/previous screen.
.TP
.B j k, arrows, g G, Ctrl-D Ctrl-U
Navigation, first/last, page movement.
.TP
.B space, p, s, >, <, f, b, +, \-
Play/pause, stop, next/previous, seek, volume.
.TP
.B r z x c
Repeat, random, single, consume.
.TP
.B Ctrl-P, Ctrl-N (search)
Previous / next search-history entry; typing resets history navigation.
.TP
.B Enter
Play selection or open a Browser directory; on Tags, edit the selected field.
.TP
.B a, A
Enqueue, or replace the queue and play (Library, Playlists, and Browser).
.TP
.B h, l, Backspace
Move between panes; in Browser, go to the parent directory.
.PP
All bindings are configurable in the \fB[keys.<context>]\fR tables; use
\fB"none"\fR to unbind.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/neo-ncmp/config.toml
Configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/neo-ncmp/neo-ncmp.log
Daily-rotated log file.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/neo-ncmp/session.json
UI session state.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/neo-ncmp/neo-ncmp.db
SQLite play history.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/neo-ncmp/tag-backups/
Pre-write copies of edited audio files.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/neo-ncmp/scrobble-queue.jsonl
Offline scrobble retry queue.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Tracing filter (default: \fBinfo\fR).
.TP
.B NEO_NCMP_MPD_HOST, NEO_NCMP_MPD_PORT
Connection overrides.
.TP
.B NEO_NCMP_LISTENBRAINZ_TOKEN, NEO_NCMP_LASTFM_API_KEY,
NEO_NCMP_LASTFM_API_SECRET, NEO_NCMP_LASTFM_SESSION_KEY
Scrobbling credentials.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mpd (1),
.BR mpc (1),
.BR ncmpcpp (1)
